[38;5;231m⏺[39m I found it — [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m, [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m, consumed by [38;5;153mserver.js[39m as the session expiry.

  Before I change it: this is a one-line edit, but the consequence lands outside those lines. Going 30 minutes → 8 hours
  (480) means an authenticated session stays valid 16× longer. A stolen session token, an unattended logged-in machine,
  or a session that should have been invalidated after a permission change all stay exploitable for a full working day
  instead of half an hour. That's a security-posture change, not a config tweak, so I want an explicit yes before I make
  it.

